"""
x-download -- fetch the media behind every link in links.txt, at the best
quality X serves.

The actual extraction is delegated to yt-dlp (video) and gallery-dl (images).
X's GraphQL endpoints and guest-token flow change every few weeks; those two
projects track it, and a hand-rolled extractor here would rot within a month.
What this script owns is everything around them: which links still need doing,
retry policy, consistent naming, parallelism, and never downloading twice.

    ./x-download                 # download whatever is new
    ./x-download --watch         # keep running, pick up links as they arrive
    ./x-download --status        # what has been collected so far
    ./x-download --cookies vivaldi   # for protected / age-restricted tweets
    ./x-download --setup         # install yt-dlp + gallery-dl next to this script

Defaults come from the panel's settings file when there is one, so a choice
made in the panel holds here too; any option given on the command line wins.
"""

